  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let $a_{1}, a_{2}, \\ldots, a_{10}$ be a G.P. If $\\frac{a_{3}}{a_{1}}=25,$ then $\\frac{a_{9}}{a_{5}}$ equals :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "hN1zi",
      "text": "$5^{4}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ogO0W",
      "text": "$4\\left(5^{2}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8nnTh",
      "text": "$5^{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "kvvoV",
      "text": "$2\\left(5^{2}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $a_{1}=a, a_{2}=a r, a_{3}=a r^{2} \\ldots a_{10}=a r^{9}$\r\n\r\nwhere $r=$ common ratio of given G.P.\r\n\r\nGiven, $\\frac{a_{3}}{a_{1}}=25$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{a r^{2}}{a}=25$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow r=\\pm 5$\r\n\r\nNow, $\\frac{a_{9}}{a_{5}}=\\frac{a r^{8}}{a r^{4}}=r^{4}=(\\pm 5)^{4}=5^{4}$",
    "image": null
  },
